%!PS
% gs -dNOSAFER

% https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intersex
% https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intersex_flag

% "...unbroken and unornamented, symbolising wholeness and
% completeness, and our potentialities. We are still fighting for
% bodily autonomy and genital integrity, and this symbolises the right
% to be who and how we want to be".
%
% The cow's head satisfies the unornamented portion but ASCII art is
% by definition a piecewise affair; wholeness may be present in spirit
% or intent but it is not physically demonstrated.
%
% > The organization describes it as freely available "for use by any
% > intersex person or organization who wishes to use it, in a human
% > rights affirming community context".[2]
%
% Arguably this should not be committed, as the author of this code is
% not intersex, and is not a member of an applicable organization.
% The author of this code intends it to affirm the human rights of
% intersex people, with a little bit of humor and nerdiness thrown in.
% The community of those who write software has always included people
% who are one or more standard deviations from the mean, in some
% dimension of their humanity.

(cowsaypride.ps) run

% The default cow head looks patently awful in this context; retain
% only the ears.
/COWTOP (^  ^) def
/COWMID (    ) def
/COWBOT (    ) def
/PAGEHEIGHT 600 def % alternate aspect ratio
/XFUDGE 0.98 def
<< /PageSize [ PAGEWIDTH PAGEHEIGHT ] >> setpagedevice

/thecircle { % --
    PAGEWIDTH 2 div
    PAGEHEIGHT 2 div
    PAGEWIDTH 6 div
    0 360 arc
    PAGEWIDTH 18 div setlinewidth
    stroke
} def

1 0 INTERSEXYELLOW stripe

newpath
INTERSEXVIOLET setrgbcolor
thecircle

cowtrace

% invert colors within cow head
typicalcowplace
1 0 INTERSEXVIOLET stripe

newpath
INTERSEXYELLOW setrgbcolor
thecircle

showpage
